00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:04.200
BETH: A range of strategies can
be used to support communication

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:07.430
and social interaction let’s
look at these in more detail.

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:11.220
JOE: PECS is a unique
alternative/augmentative communication

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:15.409
system that works for children who
do not speak, who are unintelligible

00:00:15.639 --> 00:00:17.779
or who are minimal communicators.

00:00:18.369 --> 00:00:22.759
It consists of six phases and begins by
teaching an individual to give a single

00:00:22.759 --> 00:00:28.270
picture of a desired item or action to a
“communicative partner” who immediately

00:00:28.309 --> 00:00:30.159
honours the exchange as a request.

00:00:30.689 --> 00:00:33.939
The system goes on to teach
discrimination of pictures and how

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:38.140
to put them together in ‘sentences’
and may in fact allow learners to

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:42.480
develop speech by transitioning onto
a speech generating device [SGD].

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:47.690
BETH: Makaton is a language programme
using symbols, signs and speech in spoken

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:50.019
word order, to enable communication.

00:00:50.599 --> 00:00:54.990
Signing can help those with no speech, or
those whose speech is unclear and helps

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.150
provide extra clues to what is being said.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:02.560
Symbols can help with limited speech
and cannot or prefer not to sign.

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:07.519
Makaton takes away the frustration and
enables individuals to connect with

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.489
other people and the world around them.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.840
JOE: Social stories can
help autistic people develop

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.390
greater social understanding.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:18.310
They are short descriptions of
a particular situation, event

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:22.210
or activity, and what to expect
in that situation and why.

00:01:23.059 --> 00:01:27.309
Social stories can be used to develop
self-care skills such as how to clean

00:01:27.309 --> 00:01:31.179
teeth, social skills like saying
thank you, and academic abilities.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:36.590
They present information in a literal way,
which may improve a person's understanding

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.860
of a difficult situations or activities.

00:01:39.539 --> 00:01:43.610
BETH: Music cues can be used for children
with autism as they seem to respond to

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:47.600
emotions conveyed through music better
than to other forms of communication.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:52.050
Engaging with music is thought to
help children become more flexible,

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:56.900
responsive and attentive, leading to
better social and communication skills.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:02.300
JOE: Comic strip conversations are simple
visual representations of conversation.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:05.809
They show the things that are
actually said in a conversation,

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:09.390
how people might be feeling, what
people's intentions might be.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:13.870
Comic strip conversations use stick
figures and symbols to represent

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:17.919
social interactions and abstract
aspects of conversation, and

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:21.710
colour to represent the emotional
content of a statement or message.

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:25.930
BETH: Visual supports and technology
can be used as communication

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:29.690
tools in most situations, and
are adaptable and often portable.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:33.089
They help to provide structure
and routine and improve

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.209
understanding, avoiding frustration.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:40.720
Visual supports can be real objects of
reference or tactile objects, for example

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:46.300
food labels, pictures, models, coloured
squares, symbols or written words.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:51.700
They can also be created using
technology, showing photographs, short

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:56.819
videos, pictures and symbols or actions
on a smartphone, tablet or computer.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:01.300
Visual supports however are very
personal and what works for one

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:03.570
person may not work for another.

